      "causes": ["hyp.service-incident"],
      "rationale": "A vendor incident that Microsoft posts three hours after it began. The first engineer reply sends the customer to clear caches and capture HAR traces for a problem that hit 250 users at every site at once, which is low value and a heavy ask of people working from home. The health page is clean at 11:12, which is true then, but the engineer turns it into a conclusion that it is not an outage and repeats the trace request. The incident appears at 12:05, so the health state changes between two checks (a temporal update) and the engineer withdraws the earlier view in ev10 (a correction). A health check could not have found the incident before it was posted, so the better path is about customer effort and a cautious message, not about time to the cause.",
